You may use, copy, and modify forbear (the "Software") and build it
into your own software, for free, under these rules:

1. Keep this license and the copyright notice with every copy of the
   Software.

2. Do not distribute the Software, or a modified version of it, on
   its own as a library, framework, or SDK. You may fork it for
   yourself, contribute back, and ship it inside your own Product.

   You may build and distribute your own libraries, components,
   bindings, or frameworks on top of the Software, free or paid, as
   long as the Software inside them stays under this license.

3. Do not give the Software, its code, or its tests to an AI or other
   code-generation tool to produce a framework that competes with it.

4. Royalty. If you earn Revenue from a Product, you pay 1% of its
   Revenue above USD $100,000 in each calendar year. Royalties for
   one Product never exceed USD $600,000 per year.

   A "Product" is software, or a hardware device, that you distribute
   with the Software inside it. All editions, platforms, and versions
   of the same software are one Product. If you and companies you
   control, or that control you, sell the same Product, add up the
   Revenue of all of them.

   "Revenue" is what customers pay for the Product, after sales tax,
   VAT, refunds, chargebacks, and fees kept by app stores or payment
   processors. It includes sales, subscriptions, in-app purchases,
   and ad income from the Product. For a hardware device, Revenue is
   the price of the device.

   If customers can get the Product both with and without the
   Software (for example, a desktop app built with it and a web app
   that is not), count Revenue in proportion to the share of active
   customers using a version built with the Software. If you cannot
   tell, count all of it.

   - Once a Product passes USD $100,000 in a year, email
     gabriel.readme@hey.com within 30 days.
   - Report Revenue and pay each quarter, within 45 days of the
     quarter's end. We may ask for reasonable proof of Revenue.

   No royalty is owed for:
   - software used only inside your own organization;
   - open-source products under an OSI-approved license;
   - personal projects by individuals that earn no money; or
   - non-profits using it for their mission.

   Future versions of this license may change these numbers, but
   only for versions of the Software released under the new terms.

5. While your royalties are paid up, we ship bug fixes in regular
   releases, and security patches for your major version for 18
   months after its release.

